      "103": [
        "Crafting Nonmagical Items",
        "You must use the required tool to make an item and have proficiency with that tool. Anyone who helps you must also have proficiency with it.",
        "raw materials worth half its purchase cost (round down)",
        "The GM determines whether appropriate raw materials are available.",
        "divide its purchase cost in GP by 10 (round a fraction up to a day)",
        "the days needn’t be consecutive",
        "Divide the time needed to create an item by the number of characters working on it. Normally, only one other character can assist you, but the GM might allow more assistants.",
        "Brewing Potions of Healing",
        "A character who has proficiency with the Herbalism Kit can create a Potion of Healing. Doing so requires using that kit and 25 GP of raw material over the course of 1 day (8 hours of work).",
        "Scribing Spell Scrolls",
        "For each day of inscription, you must work for 8 hours.",
        "you must have proficiency in the Arcana skill or with Calligrapher’s Supplies and have the spell prepared on each day of the inscription",
        "You must also have at hand any Material components required by the spell; if the spell consumes its Material components, they are consumed only when you complete the scroll.",
        "A spellcaster can transfer a spell to a scroll and create a Spell Scroll",
        "The GM assigns required tools for items not listed there.",
        "you make the item, and you can use it or sell it at its normal price",
        "The scroll’s spell uses your spell save DC and spell attack bonus.",
        "the version on the scroll works as if the caster were your level",
        "Spell Scroll Costs"
      ],
      "123": [
        "Detect Magic"
      ],
      "159": [
        "Level 3 Necromancy (Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger)",
        "Sacred Flame Evocation Cantrip (Cleric)",
        "Sanctuary Level 1 Abjuration (Cleric)",
        "a shard of glass from a mirror",
        "a diamond worth 300+ GP, which the spell consumes"
      ],
      "206": [
        "Crafting Magic Items",
        "“Equipment” contains rules on brewing Potions of Healing and scribing Spell Scrolls.",
        "To craft a magic item, you and any assistants must have proficiency in the Arcana skill.",
        "You must use the required tool to make an item and have proficiency with that tool. Any assistants must also have proficiency with it.",
        "The value of a Spell Scroll is double what it costs to scribe the scroll"
      ],
      "207": [
        "Magic Item Tools",
        "For each day of crafting, you must work for 8 hours. If an item requires multiple days, those days needn’t be consecutive.",
        "The cost in the table represents the raw materials needed to make a magic item. The GM determines whether appropriate raw materials are available.",
        "you must have all those spells prepared every day you spend crafting the item",
        "The time and cost are halved for a consumable item other than a Spell Scroll",
        "In a city, there is a 75 percent chance that the materials are available, and in any other settlement, that chance is 25 percent.",
        "you must wait at least 7 days before checking on the availability again",
        "you must also pay that entire cost or craft that item using the rules in “Equipment.”",
        "you must pay 3,500 GP or pay 2,000 GP and craft the armor"
      ],
      "210": [
