      "policy": "Standing gate policy set by the orchestrator: when a qualification gate (#279 or #280) is at the native cap of 100 blocked-by entries, the closed or closing splitter's own edge on the gate is replaced by the splitter's terminal qualification child. The splitter's edge carries no remaining obligation once that child exists. No other edge is removed, the count never exceeds 100, no open splitter is made blocked by a runtime implementation task, and both graphs stay acyclic.",
