  "unknowns": [
    "PDF103 does not name the unit used to round half the purchase cost down. A half that is an exact number of Copper Pieces needs no rounding; any other price needs a recorded GM amount.",
    "PDF103 and PDF207 give no rounding for crafting time divided among workers, or halved for a consumable, when the result is not a whole day. Such a project needs a recorded GM day count.",
    "PDF103 says only that the required tool must be used; it does not say what applies when two tools list one product (Club, Greatclub, Quarterstaff, Antitoxin, Holy Symbol, Arcane Focus, Druidic Focus). No executed fixture is listed twice; the products stay with the Craft roster spike.",
    "PDF103 does not say when raw materials or scribing costs are paid, and defines no refund, abandonment, check or failure for any procedure.",
    "PDF103 requires a spell prepared for scribing while cantrips are known rather than prepared.",
    "PDF103 ties 'on each day of the inscription' to preparation only. It gives no timing for having Material components at hand, except that consumed components are consumed on completion.",
    "PDF103 does not say whether a Component Pouch or Spellcasting Focus can stand in for a Material component during scribing.",
    "PDF93 lists Spell Scroll under Calligrapher's Supplies and PDF103 names only proficiency. Whether a scribe who qualifies through the supplies must hold them is not stated.",
    "PDF103 says a scribed cantrip works as if the caster were 'your level' and does not say which level a multiclass scribe uses. Only a single-class scribe executes; the question stays with the scribing coverage spike.",
    "PDF103 names the basic Potion of Healing only; brewing the stronger PDF236 variants is not stated.",
    "PDF207 does not say whether the 7-day wait after a failed availability check applies per item, per settlement or per crafter, and names no chance outside a settlement.",
    "Neither PDF103 nor PDF207 says whether a character can work two 8-hour days on one calendar day."
  ],
  "edda_adaptations": [
    "The cost is paid once, in the transaction that starts the project, through the coin payment that decision #275 assigns.",
    "A participant records at most one 8-hour workday per campaign day across all projects.",
    "A known cantrip is accepted for scribing only when it is among the scribe's own qualified Cleric cantrips on that day.",
    "A scribing workday other than the last with a Material component absent needs a recorded GM ruling; completion always requires the components.",
    "A scribe who qualifies only through Calligrapher's Supplies proficiency must hold the supplies, or have a recorded GM ruling.",
    "A Component Pouch or Spellcasting Focus does not stand in for a Material component during scribing.",
    "The saved cantrip level is the scribe's total character level, and only single-class scribes execute.",
    "A rolled availability check maps an injected percentile 1-75 to success in a city and 1-25 in another settlement, and the 7-day wait is tracked per crafter and item."
  ],
